  "stemOverrides": {
    "2": "Consider a completely full cylindrical water tank of height 1.6 m and cross-sectional area \\(0.5{\\text{ }m}^{2}\\). It has a small hole in its side at a height 90 cm from the bottom. Assume, the cross-sectional area of the hole to be negligibly small as compared to that of the water tank. If a load 50 kg is applied at the top surface of the water in the tank then the velocity of the water coming out at the instant when the hole is opened is : \\(\\left( g= 10\\text{ }m/s^{2} \\right)\\)\\",
    "3": "Choose the correct logic circuit for the given truth table having inputs A and B.\n\n| A | B | Y |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0 | 0 | 0 |\n| 0 | 1 | 0 |\n| 1 | 0 | 1 |\n| 1 | 1 | 1 |",
    "9": "Match the LIST-I with LIST-II\n\n| LIST-I | LIST-II |\n|---|---|\n| A. Gravitational constant | I. \\(\\left[LT^{-2}\\right]\\) |\n| B. Gravitational potential energy | II. \\(\\left[L^{2}T^{-2}\\right]\\) |\n| C. Gravitational potential | III. \\(\\left[ML^{2}T^{-2}\\right]\\) |\n| D. Acceleration due to gravity | IV. \\(\\left[M^{-1}L^{3}T^{-2}\\right]\\) |\n\nChoose the correct answer from the options given below:",
    "13": "Match the LIST-I with LIST-II\n\n| LIST-I | LIST-II |\n|---|---|\n| A. \\(^{1}_{0}n + ^{235}_{92}U \\rightarrow\\ ^{140}_{54}Xe + ^{94}_{38}Sr + 2\\,^{1}_{0}n\\) | I. Chemical reaction |\n| B. \\(2H_{2} + O_{2} \\rightarrow 2H_{2}O\\) | II. Fusion with +ve Q value |\n| C. \\(^{2}_{1}H + ^{2}_{1}H \\rightarrow\\ ^{3}_{2}He + ^{1}_{0}n\\) | III. Fission |\n| D. \\(^{1}_{1}H + ^{3}_{1}H \\rightarrow\\ ^{2}_{1}H + ^{2}_{1}H\\) | IV. Fusion with -ve Q value |\n\nChoose the correct answer from the options given below:",
    "51": "Let \\(A\\) be a matrix of order \\(3\\times 3\\) and \\(|A|=5\\). If \\(|2\\,\\mathrm{adj}(3A\\,\\mathrm{adj}(2A))|=2^{\\alpha}\\cdot3^{\\beta}\\cdot5^{\\gamma},\\ \\alpha,\\beta,\\gamma\\in N\\), then \\(\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma\\) is equal to",
    "55": "Let \\(A=\\{-3,-2,-1,0,1,2,3\\}\\). Let \\(R\\) be a relation on \\(A\\) defined by \\(xRy\\) if and only if \\(0\\leq x^{2}+2y\\leq 4\\). Let \\(l\\) be the number of elements in \\(R\\) and \\(m\\) be the minimum number of elements required to be added in \\(R\\) to make it a reflexive relation. Then \\(l+m\\) is equal to.",
    "75": "The area of the region bounded by the curve \\(y=\\max\\{|x|,\\ x|x-2|\\}\\), the \\(x\\)-axis and the lines \\(x=-2\\) and \\(x=4\\) is equal to",
    "91": "Match the LIST-I with LIST-II\n\n| LIST-I | LIST-II |\n|---|---|\n| A. Boltzmann constant | I. \\(\\left[ML^{2}T^{-1}\\right]\\) |\n| B. Coefficient of viscosity | II. \\(\\left[MLT^{-3}K^{-1}\\right]\\) |\n| C. Planck's constant | III. \\(\\left[ML^{2}T^{-2}K^{-1}\\right]\\) |\n| D. Thermal conductivity | IV. \\(\\left[ML^{-1}T^{-1}\\right]\\) |\n\nChoose the correct answer from the options given below:"
  },
  "notes": "2025 3 Apr sitting — 2025 layout (Maths Q51-75 + Q126-150 = 50 q). Clean number-matched keys. Q51 RTL-formatted options (25/26/27/28) + answer C=27; Q56 no-token block value-matched to 338=D; Q140 answer A=0 (equilateral centroid identity); Q75 'Physics' leak stripped.",
  "authoredSolutions": {
    "56": "Put \\(x=\\sqrt5+r\\cos\\theta,\\ y=\\sqrt5+r\\sin\\theta\\) into \\(25x^2+36y^2=900\\): \\[(25\\cos^2\\theta+36\\sin^2\\theta)r^2+\\sqrt5(50\\cos\\theta+72\\sin\\theta)r-595=0.\\] Then \\(PA\\cdot PB=\\dfrac{595}{25+11\\sin^2\\theta}\\), maximum when \\(\\sin\\theta=0\\) (denominator \\(25\\)). With \\(\\sin\\theta=0,\\ \\cos\\theta=\\pm1\\): \\(r_1r_2=-\\frac{119}{5}\\), \\(r_1+r_2=\\mp2\\sqrt5\\). Hence \\(PA^2+PB^2=(r_1+r_2)^2-2r_1r_2=20+\\frac{238}{5}=\\frac{338}{5}\\), so \\(5(PA^2+PB^2)=338.\\)",
    "140": "Place the centroid at the origin by writing \\(w_{k} = z_{k} - z_{0}\\), so that \\(w_{1}+w_{2}+w_{3} = 0\\). For an equilateral triangle centred at the origin the vertices are a common radius times the three cube roots of unity, \\(w_{k} = r\\omega^{k}\\) with \\(1 + \\omega + \\omega^{2} = 0\\). Then \\[\\sum_{k=1}^{3}\\left( z_{k}-z_{0} \\right)^{2} = \\sum_{k=1}^{3} w_{k}^{2} = r^{2}\\left( 1 + \\omega^{2} + \\omega^{4} \\right)\\] and since \\(\\omega^{4} = \\omega\\), the bracket is \\(1 + \\omega + \\omega^{2} = 0\\). Hence the sum is \\(0\\) and the correct choice is A. Equivalently, \\(\\sum w_{k}^{2} = \\left( \\sum w_{k} \\right)^{2} - 2\\sum_{i<j} w_{i}w_{j}\\), and both terms vanish for an equilateral triangle centred at the origin. [Source note: option (b) is printed BLANK in the source paper itself — verified against the original document, not an extraction fault. The correct answer 0 is option (a) and is unaffected, so the question is answerable as it stands.]"
  },
